{"t": 1794112721.6736555, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Fixed the red `contract-tests` check on this branch.\n\n**What failed:** `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` \u2014 `fee(2.675)` returned `2.67` instead of `2.68`.\n\n**Why:** the float implementation (`round(amount * 0.01 * 100, 2)`) rounds the binary float value of `2.675`, which is really `2.67499999...`, so it rounds down instead of up. That breaks the card-network contract in PAY-88: fees must be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents; binary float rounding is not acceptable.\n\n**What I changed** (`payments/fees.py`): compute on exact decimal values and quantize with `ROUND_HALF_UP` instead of using float `round()`:\n\n```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\nexact = Decimal(str(amount)) * Decimal(\"0.01\") * Decimal(\"100\")\nreturn float(exact.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```\n\nVerified locally: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, and the existing assertions (`fee(100.0) == 100.0`) still pass. Pushed as a new commit on `fees-float`.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794112755.121747, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_pull_request_read", "args": {"method": "get_check_runs", "owner": "acme", "pullNumber": 214, "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
